In X-bar theory, the prepositional phrase (PP) "on Saturday" can be structurally attached at two different points in the syntactic derivation, resulting in two distinct meanings:

1. **High Attachment (VP-Adjunct to the matrix clause):** The PP adjoins to the intermediate projection of the matrix verb (*swore*). In this parse, the act of swearing (making a promise/oath) occurred on Saturday. 
