In this phrase, the participle/adjective "flying" modifies the noun "objects" (creating an adjective-modified noun). The adjective "Unidentified" then recursively modifies that entire adjective-modified noun phrase ("flying objects"). In X-bar theory, this is captured by the recursive phrase structure rule **N′ → AP N′**, where an N′ can contain another N′ of the same category, allowing for potentially infinite pre-nominal modification.

