In this expanded sentence, the noun "journalist" is modified by another embedded relative clause, *"who covered the case"*. This creates a recursive structure where a clause (CP2: *who covered the case*) is embedded within a noun phrase (NP2: *journalist*), which is itself part of an embedded clause (CP1: *every journalist who covered the case questioned*), which in turn is embedded within the main noun phrase (NP1: *The expert...*), ultimately sitting within the main clause (TP: *The expert... remained completely silent*).

